{
  "summary": "Adds an optional transaction output script index (`txoscriptindex`) that indexes script pubkeys by a six-byte SipHash prefix of their SHA256 hash alongside an order-preserving `OrderedVarInt` block height. Introduces a `getscripthistory` RPC allowing queries for transaction outputs and spending transactions by script hash, address, or ranged descriptor across a block height window. It also exposes transaction byte offsets in `txospenderindex` and extracts common transaction JSON rendering helpers for raw transaction RPCs.",
  "problem": "Bitcoin Core cannot query historical transactions by address or script without importing them into an active wallet descriptor set. External wallets, Electrum servers, and explorers must run and maintain separate, resource-intensive third-party indexing software to track script activity.",
  "evidence": [
    "Address and script indexing has been requested and attempted in at least five closed PRs dating back to 2013 (#2802, #3652, #6835, #10370, #14053).",
    "Author reports that the new index requires ~54 GB of disk space (less than v31 `txindex`), syncs in a few hours, and functions on pruned nodes with missing blocks fetchable via peer requests."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
   "depends_on": [],
   "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Adds a new optional index subclass and serialization format (`OrderedVarIntFormatter`), alongside over 1,000 lines of functional tests and unit tests. The PR also touches `txospenderindex` to expose transaction byte offsets and refactors `TxToJSON` and doc generators across raw transaction RPCs.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Updated the SipHash prefix size from five bytes to six bytes, raising expected index storage requirements from ~52 GB to ~54 GB.",
  "card": "Adds an optional txoscriptindex and a getscripthistory RPC to query transaction outputs and spenders by address, Electrum script hash, or ranged descriptor across a block height window. Bitcoin Core cannot currently look up script history without wallet descriptors, forcing users and Electrum servers to run external indexer daemons. Address and script indexing has been requested and closed in at least five PRs since 2013. The author states the index requires ~54 GB of disk space, syncs in a few hours, and supports pruned nodes.",
